"notes": "Fix pass (attempt 5). Cash-basis village; governmental statement is cash-basis rev/exp/fund balance (p4), total column. Governmental roll-forward: transfers net (10,544) entered as transfers_out; donations 3,000 as other_financing; reconciles to 725,674 with line items (p3 prints 725,673). Debt Service expenditure line is 0 and omitted. Public buildings mapped to general government. Business-type taken from Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Fund Balances - Proprietary Funds (p6), which includes depreciation; measure = net position. No single printed business-type receipts total; 652,049 = printed total operating revenues 651,706 + interest income 343 (excludes transfers net 10,543); the receipt line items add to 652,048 because the printed 651,706 is $1 above 647,580 + 4,125. Business disbursements total 724,425 as printed on p2 (items sum 724,424). Report itself does not add up by small amounts (see report_discrepancies). Detail: General Fund revenues from the p7 budget schedule; General Fund expenditures from the p10 combining schedule by object (Total column, all sub-funds, printed total 1,375,300, excludes the transfer), so the p7 function-total expenditure lines are not recorded (no double counting); the p7 transfer out (-10,544) is kept as other financing. Budget columns on pp7-9 are headed 'Budget (Original)' and recorded as budget_final. Detail totals 659,935 and 637,804 as printed (items foot to 659,936 / 637,805). Motor vehicle fees under Intergovernmental kept as state aid (motor vehicle pro-rate); wheel tax and Taxes: Motor vehicle classed motor vehicle tax. Utility sales on p9 not split water vs sewer."
